.TH tuexpand n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuexpand
.PP
\fBexpand\fR/\fBunexpand\fR\-like conversion between tabs and spaces in pure Tcl, with correct tab\-stop alignment.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tuexpand::expand   text ?-tabs N?
::tclutils::tuexpand::unexpand text ?-tabs N? ?-all 0|1?
::tclutils::tuexpand::file     path ?-mode expand|unexpand? ?-tabs N? ?-all 0|1?
.CE
.PP
\fB\-tabs\fR sets the tab width (default 8). \fB\-all\fR belongs to \fBunexpand\fR only; \fBexpand\fR rejects it as an unknown option.
.PP
\fBunexpand\fR converts only the leading blanks (spaces and tabs) by default and copies the rest of the line unchanged, so tabs inside the line stay tabs. \fB\-all 1\fR converts every run of blanks. Within a run of two or more blanks, or a run at the start of the line, each tab stop the run reaches becomes a tab; the spaces left after the last stop stay spaces. A single space inside the line stays a space, also right before a tab stop. Spaces right before a tab are absorbed by it. This matches GNU \fBunexpand\fR (\fB\-a\fR for \fB\-all 1\fR).
.CS
::tclutils::tuexpand::unexpand "a\tb"                       ;# -> a\tb
::tclutils::tuexpand::unexpand "abcdefg          x" -all 1  ;# -> abcdefg\t\t x
.CE
.SS Errors
.TS
l l.
Case	\fB\-errorcode\fR
\fBfile\fR: unknown \fB\-mode\fR	\fB{TCLUTILS TUEXPAND MODE}\fR
\fBfile\fR: \fB\-mode\fR without value	\fB{TCLUTILS TUEXPAND OPTION}\fR
unknown option (also \fB\-all\fR for \fBexpand\fR)	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION \-name}\fR
\fB\-tabs\fR not a positive integer	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON INTEGER \-tabs}\fR
\fB\-all\fR not a boolean	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-all}\fR
.TE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tuexpand.tcl -tabs 4 file.txt
tclsh bin/tuexpand.tcl unexpand -all 1 file.txt
.CE
